      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the next week, closely monitor your heifer for signs of infection, such as continued fever, lethargy, profuse discharge from the incision, or severe abdominal pain. Be vigilant about appetite and water intake; a sudden refusal to eat or drink is a red flag. For diet, keep her diet highly digestible and easily managed—start with small amounts of palatable, high-quality feed and gradually reintroduce her normal ration as she improves. If you notice any worsening symptoms, contact your veterinarian immediately for guidance.",
