    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. what specifically should i be looking for around the incision site? i want to make sure there isn't anything nasty going on under the skin or inside that i can't see yet. like, how do i tell the difference between normal healing and something more serious starting to develop internally?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Externally, watch for unusual swelling, excessive redness spreading from the incision, or any signs of warmth or heat radiating around the stitches. Pus discharge, characterized by thick, foul-smelling, or cloudy drainage, is a major indicator of infection needing immediate attention. Slight pinkish-tinged seepage is often normal, but any persistent weeping or discharge that changes color or odor warrants a vet call. Internal complications are harder to see, so any sudden drop in appetite or change in condition should prompt a veterinary checkup.",
      "source": "target",
